AB  - Introduction: Intense pulsed light (IPL) treatment has become very popular in India. However, there is limited literature regarding its use for pigmentary lesions in Indian skin.Objectives: To evaluate the safety and effectiveness of IPL in the treatment of pigmentary disorders in Indian patients.Methods: IPL treatment was offered to 11 Indian patients with pigmentary disorders.Results: Good outcomes were observed in patients with lentigines, freckles, and post-acne pigmentation. No serious adverse effects were reported.Conclusions: IPL appears to be a safe and effective treatment option for selected pigmentary disorders in Indian skin.
